Speed up render-to-texture (motion blur) cutscenes (e.g. Alone in the Dark: The
New Nightmare) that otherwise run at roughly half speed (slow motion + slow audio).

These cutscenes issue an extra render-to-texture pass per frame. In threaded
rendering the emulation thread blocks (re.Wait) until that RTT render finishes on
the GPU, which serializes the ~14ms RTT render with emulation and roughly halves
the emulated Dreamcast clock (vblanks drop from ~60 to ~30/s).

When RenderToTextureBuffer is disabled the SH4 never reads back the RTT pixels
(the result stays a GL texture resolved on the render thread, in order), so the
emulation thread does not need to wait for GPU completion. Release the emulation
thread early for RTT frames in that case (as is already done for visible frames),
letting the RTT render overlap with emulation. When RenderToTextureBuffer is on,
keep the original synchronous behaviour.

Note: with the single-slot render queue this may occasionally drop a frame under
load (minor visual glitch) in exchange for full speed; a glitch-free version would
require a deeper render-pipeline rework.

--- a/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp	2026-09-11 22:20:10.377986213 +0200
+++ b/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp	2026-09-11 22:20:10.380110964 +0200
@@ -168,11 +168,14 @@
    }
    bool proc = renderer->Process(ctx);
 #if !defined(TARGET_NO_THREADS)
-   if (settings.rend.ThreadedRendering && (!proc || (!ctx->rend.isRenderFramebuffer && !ctx->rend.isRTT)))
-	   // If rendering to texture, continue locking until the frame is rendered
+   // AE: RTT normalerweise synchron abwarten. Bei RenderToTextureBuffer=off liest die SH4
+   // die RTT-Pixel nicht -> async freigeben (Render-Thread rendert RTT+sichtbar in Reihenfolge),
+   // damit der 14ms-RTT-Render die Emulation nicht seriell blockiert (Cutscene-Slowdown).
+   bool rttAsync = ctx->rend.isRTT && !settings.rend.RenderToTextureBuffer;
+   if (settings.rend.ThreadedRendering && (!proc || (!ctx->rend.isRenderFramebuffer && (!ctx->rend.isRTT || rttAsync))))
       re.Set();
 #endif
-   
+
    bool do_swp = proc && renderer->Render();
 
    return do_swp;
@@ -220,7 +223,7 @@
 		swap_pending = do_swp && !_pvrrc->rend.isRenderFramebuffer && FB_R_SOF1 != FB_W_SOF1
 				 && settings.rend.ThreadedRendering && settings.rend.DelayFrameSwapping;
 
-		if (settings.rend.ThreadedRendering && _pvrrc->rend.isRTT)
+		if (settings.rend.ThreadedRendering && _pvrrc->rend.isRTT && settings.rend.RenderToTextureBuffer)
 			re.Set();
 
